PROJECT TITLE:
Mini Shell – Operating System Project

PROJECT DESCRIPTION:
The Mini Shell project is a simple command-line interface that demonstrates
basic operating system concepts. It allows users to enter commands and
interact with the system through a shell. The project focuses on understanding
process creation, command execution, system calls, and basic shell operations.

EXPECTED OUTCOMES:
1. Develop a basic working mini shell.
2. Execute basic commands entered by the user.
3. Understand process creation and process management.
4. Learn how system calls are used in operating systems.
5. Implement basic command parsing and execution.
6. Gain practical knowledge of Linux/Operating System concepts.
